### 6\. Conclusion

The Quick Sort algorithm was successfully implemented using the Divide and Conquer strategy. The program selects a pivot element and partitions the array into smaller subarrays. These subarrays are sorted recursively until the complete array is arranged in ascending order. The execution time required for sorting the elements is also calculated and displayed.

### 7\. Time and Space Complexity

| Case         | Time Complexity |
| ------------ | --------------- |
| Best Case    | O(n log n)      |
| Average Case | O(n log n)      |
| Worst Case   | O(n²)           |

Space Complexity: O(log n) on average for the recursion stack.

Important for viva: The worst case occurs when the pivot repeatedly becomes the smallest or largest element, resulting in highly unbalanced partitions.
